Node-testable surface (what got a test)
---------------------------------------
The dim-tick <marker> def renders inside a hidden <svg><defs> in GraphCanvas.
The suite already carries an OPPORTUNISTIC GraphCanvas SSR row (smoke.test.tsx,
"GraphCanvas SSR (opportunistic bonus — Stage 3 P2)") that renders GraphCanvas
via renderToStaticMarkup in node. That SSR reaches the defs block, so the
marker's PRESENCE is node-assertable:

  smoke.test.tsx :: "renders the dimension-tick marker def (Stage 9 P1 Axis 2)"
    expect(html).toContain('id="dim-tick"')

Note vs. the dispatch brief: the brief anticipated GraphCanvas might be
smoke-EXCLUDED (no SSR row possible). In the live suite GraphCanvas IS rendered
by the opportunistic SSR bonus row, so the def IS reachable and the brief's
PRIMARY instruction (add one smoke row pinning the marker defs presence IF
reachable by SSR) applies. The def's rendered LOOK (45° tick, size, ink colour)
remains walk-gated — only its presence is pinned.

